# Pull request as soon as you edit

When this session starts changing files in a git repo, open a pull request right after the first edit. Do not wait until the work is finished. Push later changes to the same branch so the pull request tracks the work as it goes. Questions that do not edit files stop with no pull request.

**Done when:** `gh pr view --json url,baseRefName` returns a URL whose `baseRefName` equals `integrationBranch`, or the session changed no files.

1. Read `integrationBranch` from `.cursor/agent-manifest.json`. If it is missing or empty, ask once and stop. Do not guess `dev`, `staging`, or `main`.
2. Stay in the current worktree when its branch is not `integrationBranch`. A host worktree counts. Create a new worktree only when the checkout is `integrationBranch` itself. Do not commit on `integrationBranch`.
3. After the first edit, commit the files this session changed and push. Open the pull request with `gh pr create --draft --base <integrationBranch>` when `gh pr view` does not already show one. Commit and push again after each further round of edits.
4. If `git diff origin/<integrationBranch>...HEAD` is empty, stop. There is nothing to review.
5. When the work is done, mark the pull request ready with `gh pr ready`.

Skip the pull request only when the user says not to open one.
